@meta
id: 18-03
title: Drill — Tab down the tree
chapter: 18
type: drill
skills: edit-file, wildmenu
par: 40
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: Ctrl+P, "cusent", Enter
vimrc: set wildmenu wildmode=longest:full,full
open: README.md

@brief
Eight times: from the README, open the customer entity at
`src/domain/customer/customer.entity.ts` using one letter and one Tab per
level, fix `emial` to `email`, save, quit.

The last level is the interesting one. `c` Tab gives you `customer.` and
stops, because three files start that way. One more letter and one more
Tab finishes it.

@keys
| `Tab` | complete as far as is unambiguous |
| `:e` | edit |

@hints
`:e s<Tab>d<Tab>c<Tab>` gets you to `src/domain/customer/`. Then
`c<Tab>` fills in `customer.` and waits.
--
`e<Tab>` picks `customer.entity.ts` from the three. `/emial`, `ciw`,
`email`, done.

@solution
    :e s<Tab>d<Tab>c<Tab>c<Tab>e<Tab><Enter>
    /emial<Enter> ciwemail <Esc> :wq<Enter>

The rhythm is letter, Tab, letter, Tab. When Tab stops short, look at
the bar, add the letter that settles it, Tab again. By the eighth rep
you should not be reading the bar at all for the directories, only for
the file.

@start README.md
# Orders service

    src/domain/<name>/<name>.entity.ts       the shape of a record
    src/domain/<name>/<name>.repository.ts   how it is loaded and saved
    src/domain/<name>/<name>.provider.ts     the business rules

@start src/domain/customer/customer.entity.ts
export type Customer = {
  id: string;
  emial: string;
  name: string;
};

@expected src/domain/customer/customer.entity.ts
export type Customer = {
  id: string;
  email: string;
  name: string;
};

@start src/domain/customer/customer.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { CustomerRepository } from './customer.repository';

@injectable()
export class CustomerProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(CustomerRepository) protected customerRepository: CustomerRepository,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const customer = await this.customerRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!customer) {
      throw exception('CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return customer;
  }
}

@start src/domain/customer/customer.repository.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { Customer as CustomerRecord } from '@prisma/client';
import { BaseRepository } from '../../infrastructure/base.repository';
import { Customer } from './customer.entity';

@injectable()
export class CustomerRepository extends BaseRepository<CustomerRecord, Customer> {
  public toEntity(record: CustomerRecord): Customer {
    return {
      id: record.id,
      email: record.email,
      name: record.name,
    };
  }
}

@start src/domain/order/order.entity.ts
export type Order = {
